### C++ Code Example

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <fstream>
#include <sstream>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <json/json.h> // Make sure to include the jsoncpp library

// Function to split a string by a given delimiter
std::vector<std::string> split(const std::string &s, char delimiter) {
    std::vector<std::string> tokens;
    std::stringstream ss(s);
    std::string token;

    while (std::getline(ss, token, delimiter)) {
        tokens.push_back(token);
    }
    return tokens;
}

// Function to convert CSV to JSON
void convertCsvToJson(const std::string &inputFile, const std::string &outputFile) {
    std::ifstream csvFile(inputFile);
    std::ofstream jsonFile(outputFile);

    if (!csvFile.is_open() || !jsonFile.is_open()) {
        std::cerr << "Error opening files!" << std::endl;
        return;
    }

    std::string line;
    std::getline(csvFile, line); // Read header line
    std::vector<std::string> headers = split(line, ','); // Split headers

    Json::Value jsonData(Json::arrayValue); // Create JSON array

    // Read each line of the CSV file
    while (std::getline(csvFile, line)) {
        std::vector<std::string> values = split(line, ',');
        Json::Value jsonObject;

        for (size_t i = 0; i < headers.size(); ++i) {
            jsonObject[headers[i]] = values[i]; // Assign values to headers
        }
        jsonData.append(jsonObject); // Add object to JSON array
    }

    // Write JSON data to file
    jsonFile << jsonData;

    csvFile.close();
    jsonFile.close();
}

int main() {
    std::string inputFile = "input.csv"; // Specify your input CSV file
    std::string outputFile = "output.json"; // Specify your output JSON file

    convertCsvToJson(inputFile, outputFile);
    std::cout << "CSV has been converted to JSON successfully!" << std::endl;

    return 0;
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **Includes and Libraries**: The code uses `<fstream>` for file handling, `<sstream>` for string manipulation, and `<json/json.h>` for working with JSON. Make sure you have the jsoncpp library installed.

2. **Function `split`**: This function takes a string and a delimiter character, splits the string at each occurrence of the delimiter, and returns a vector of the resulting substrings.

3. **Function `convertCsvToJson`**: 
   - It opens the specified CSV file for reading and a JSON file for writing.
   - It reads the first line of the CSV to get the headers and splits them into a vector.
   - It then reads the rest of the lines, splits each line into values, and maps these values to the corresponding headers, creating a JSON object for each row.
   - Finally, it appends each JSON object to a JSON array and writes the entire array to the output JSON file.

4. **Main Function**: Specifies the input and output file paths and calls the conversion function.

### Note:
- Before running this code, make sure to install the jsoncpp library and link it correctly in your project.
- Adjust the input and output file paths as needed.
